    privacyPolicyBody: "## What we store\n- Account: email, name, and how you sign in (email or Google).\n- Finance data you enter: transactions, accounts and balances, debts/receivables, budgets, savings goals, trips, recurring items and notes.\n- Receipt photos/screenshots you scan, kept in private storage that only your account can open.\n- Ask Revi chat history and a count of AI feature use (to count credits).\n- Notification subscription (if you turn it on) and the feedback/reviews you send from the Support menu.\n\n## What we use it for\nTo run the app: show your numbers, sync across devices, send the reminders you enabled, count AI credits and respond to your feedback. Your data is not sold and not used for advertising.\n\n## Who helps process it\n- Supabase: database, sign-in, file storage and the app's servers.\n- Netlify: hosts the app.\n- Google: Google sign-in; Gmail Sync (read-only access to bank notification emails, only if you connect it yourself); and the Gemini AI service. When you use Scan Receipt, Voice Add, Split Bill or Ask Revi, the photo/text/summary needed for that request is sent to Google's AI to be processed.\n- Exchange-rate and market-price providers: only currency or asset codes, no personal data.\n- Payments (when available) are handled by a third-party payment provider; we never store your card number.\n\n## Google and Gmail data\nRevinance's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the Google API Services User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements. If you connect Gmail, we only read bank notification emails to help record transactions at your request. Email contents are not sold, not used for advertising and not used to train general AI models. You can disconnect Gmail at any time.\n\n## Your control\n- Export: Settings → Data → Export JSON, anytime.\n- Delete your data: send it from Settings → Support → Feature Request and choose \"Delete my data\". We delete your account and all its data as soon as possible, within 30 days at most.\n- You can disconnect Gmail and turn off notifications at any time.\n\n## Security and retention\nData travels over encrypted connections (HTTPS) and each account can only access its own data. Data is kept while your account is active and deleted when you ask. No system is 100% secure, so please protect your account access.\n\n## Children\nRevinance is not intended for anyone under 18.\n\n## Changes\nThis policy may be updated. Important changes will be announced in the app. Last updated: October 2026.",
    termsBody: "## About Revinance\nRevinance is a personal finance tracking tool that is still in beta. Features may change and the service may occasionally be interrupted. Export your data regularly as a backup.\n\n## Not financial advice\nEvery number, suggestion and insight (including from Ask Revi) is only meant to help you calculate and stay on track. It is not professional financial, legal or tax advice. Your financial decisions remain your responsibility.\n\n## AI results can be wrong\nScan Receipt, Voice Add, Split Bill, Gmail Sync and Ask Revi use AI. Results can be mistaken, so check amounts, dates and categories before saving or acting on them.\n\n## Account, AI credits and plans\n- You are responsible for your account and the data you enter, which must be accurate and yours to use.\n- AI features use monthly credits depending on your plan. Scan Receipt uses 1 credit per receipt that is successfully read; receipts that cannot be read are not charged.\n- Trials and Pro codes are personal, one code per account, and may be withdrawn if abused.\n- Prices and plan limits may change with notice in the app.\n\n## Fair use\nDo not use Revinance for anything unlawful, to disrupt the service, or to try to access anyone else's data.\n\n## Termination\nYou can stop using Revinance at any time and ask for your data to be deleted. We may suspend accounts that break these terms.\n\n## Limitation of liability\nTo the extent permitted by law, the service is provided \"as is\" and Revinance is not liable for indirect losses or losses caused by wrong figures, AI results or service interruptions.\n\n## Governing law\nThese terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Indonesia. Last updated: October 2026.",
